[[systemd: Writing Unit Files]]

* systemd Writing unit files: creating a .service file so an app starts on boot, restarts on failure, runs as a specific user, and starts after the network or database is up (After=, Requires=, Restart=).

|!Section |!Question |!Examples |
|`[Unit]` |When and in what order? |`Description=`, `After=`, `Wants=`, `Requires=` |
|`[Service]` |How do I run it? |`ExecStart=`, `User=`, `Restart=`, `Type=` |
|`[Install]` |Where does enable hook it in? |`WantedBy=multi-user.target` |